tags: network-bytes-per-day

A limit of the node: the most bytes that the node relays through ServiceTunnel in one day, for all the clients together.

The value is an integer in bytes. Example: 107374182400. The day is from 00:00 to 24:00 UTC. When the node has no bytes left, it refuses the traffic with RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=network-bytes-per-day
per=all the clients of the node together
rule=The day is from 00:00 to 24:00 UTC. When the node has no bytes left, it refuses the traffic with RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED.
scope=none
unit=bytes
